There's nowhere to put it though.

806
00:45:36,140 --> 00:45:37,140
Oh, that won't work.

807
00:45:37,140 --> 00:45:40,070
We're sunk.

808
00:45:40,070 --> 00:45:41,870
Huh?

809
00:45:41,870 --> 00:45:43,670
What are we supposed to do?

810
00:45:43,670 --> 00:45:46,210
We need to make a light bridge cube?

811
00:45:46,210 --> 00:45:49,680
A loop cube?

812
00:45:49,680 --> 00:45:51,980
A loop cube?

813
00:45:51,980 --> 00:45:52,900
I messed up.

814
00:45:52,900 --> 00:45:53,540
Huh?

815
00:45:53,540 --> 00:45:57,220
Ponpon, don't grab the square one.

816
00:45:57,220 --> 00:45:58,220
How do you grab the square one?

817
00:45:58,220 --> 00:45:58,880
Oh, this?

818
00:45:58,880 --> 00:46:00,720
Hey, all of a sudden—

819
00:46:00,720 --> 00:46:03,840
Don't suddenly start acting all realistic on me.

820
00:46:03,840 --> 00:46:04,340
Okay!

821
00:46:04,340 --> 00:46:07,180
Isn't that a light bridge cube? Is that okay?

822
00:46:07,180 --> 00:46:09,640
This isn't a light bridge one.

823
00:46:09,640 --> 00:46:10,140
Yep.

824
00:46:10,140 --> 00:46:10,640
Amazing.

825
00:46:10,640 --> 00:46:12,280
Hmm, how do we do this?

826
00:46:12,280 --> 00:46:15,360
We probably need to use that thing down below somehow.

827
00:46:15,360 --> 00:46:18,020
So we use the one down there.

828
00:46:18,020 --> 00:46:21,000
With this, probably—

829
00:46:21,000 --> 00:46:22,340
Wheee!

830
00:46:22,340 --> 00:46:24,040
Wheee!

831
00:46:24,040 --> 00:46:25,400
Wheee!

832
00:46:25,400 --> 00:46:27,260
How do you do it?

833
00:46:27,260 --> 00:46:31,620
How do you go "wheee"? With this?

834
00:46:31,620 --> 00:46:33,100
Oh, maybe—

835
00:46:33,100 --> 00:46:35,580
Do this here and here—

836
00:46:35,580 --> 00:46:39,410
And then—

837
00:46:39,410 --> 00:46:41,690
Huh?

838
00:46:41,690 --> 00:46:42,870
Can't reach?

839
00:46:42,870 --> 00:46:45,740
Just now, something… huh?

840
00:46:45,740 --> 00:46:47,750
The momentum keeps getting weaker and weaker.

841
00:46:47,750 --> 00:46:49,910
Won't it become an infinite loop? Huh?

842
00:46:49,910 --> 00:46:51,010
It's not becoming an infinite loop.

843
00:46:51,010 --> 00:46:53,530
I feel like the idea itself is great though.

844
00:46:53,530 --> 00:46:56,210
What if we destroy that thing over there?

845
00:46:56,210 --> 00:46:59,090
Oh, but if we destroy that, then we can't...

846
00:46:59,090 --> 00:47:01,470
Ugh, is it hopeless?

847
00:47:01,470 --> 00:47:04,050
What are we supposed to do?

848
00:47:04,050 --> 00:47:05,850
We need more momentum.

849
00:47:05,850 --> 00:47:07,690
So it has to be the refraction cube after all?

850
00:47:07,690 --> 00:47:10,270
I want to use the refraction cube to smash through, but—

851
00:47:10,270 --> 00:47:14,430
I just don't know where to refract it.

852
00:47:14,430 --> 00:47:17,450
What are you even talking about?

853
00:47:17,450 --> 00:47:22,370
Because the way we've been using the cube so far—

854
00:47:22,370 --> 00:47:25,150
It just doesn't reach.

855
00:47:25,150 --> 00:47:27,610
I really need that momentum to keep going.

856
00:47:27,610 --> 00:47:31,070
Would opening up the one on the right even help?

857
00:47:31,070 --> 00:47:32,390
Both are pointing down, so probably not.

858
00:47:32,390 --> 00:47:34,610
We need one that goes upward.

859
00:47:34,610 --> 00:47:35,990
If we could open that one—

860
00:47:35,990 --> 00:47:42,390
Something that would send us upward—

861
00:47:42,390 --> 00:47:44,970
Like, up to the stars—

862
00:47:44,970 --> 00:47:47,650
Something that goes up.

863
00:47:47,650 --> 00:47:54,550
Actually, the heights are slightly different, so—

864
00:47:54,550 --> 00:47:56,390
Maybe if it's this one, we can make it.

865
00:47:56,390 --> 00:47:59,940
Nope.

866
00:47:59,940 --> 00:48:04,400
Plus there's a ceiling over there.

867
00:48:04,400 --> 00:48:07,200
What about connecting it to the middle one?

868
00:48:07,200 --> 00:48:11,000
Connect it to the middle? Where, where?

869
00:48:11,000 --> 00:48:14,600
From partway through to here… here?

870
00:48:14,600 --> 00:48:18,200
Like connecting here and here.

871
00:48:18,200 --> 00:48:26,600
Take what falls from here, connect it here, then connect it here?

872
00:48:26,600 --> 00:48:27,600
Yes, yes, exactly!

873
00:48:31,000 --> 00:48:35,250
The momentum… those things are just floating around.

874
00:48:35,250 --> 00:48:38,960
I don't think the momentum changes though.

875
00:48:38,960 --> 00:48:41,760
There's a ceiling over there.

876
00:48:41,760 --> 00:48:43,140
A ceiling?

877
00:48:43,140 --> 00:48:44,740
Which one is the ceiling?

878
00:48:44,740 --> 00:48:47,560
Look, there's a ceiling right here.

879
00:48:47,560 --> 00:48:53,170
There's a ceiling here.

880
00:48:53,170 --> 00:48:56,050
Okay, let's just go for it.

881
00:48:56,050 --> 00:48:57,350
Yeah, you're right.

882
00:48:59,150 --> 00:49:06,690
Connect that one to this one, but right now we're just floating around...

883
00:49:06,690 --> 00:49:13,150
If we teleport somewhere, it looks like it's falling right now.

884
00:49:13,150 --> 00:49:15,330
Alright then.

885
00:49:15,330 --> 00:49:20,310
It stopped over there in a weird spot.

886
00:49:20,310 --> 00:49:25,490
It ended up in a weird spot... how do we get past this?

887
00:49:25,490 --> 00:49:29,610
Nice, nice! Come on over!

888
00:49:29,610 --> 00:49:31,870
Do it here! I'll try my best.

889
00:49:31,870 --> 00:49:34,910
Wait, was it here before?

890
00:49:34,910 --> 00:49:40,530
If we connect that to that... the distance isn't enough.

891
00:49:40,530 --> 00:49:49,350
Over here... yeah, it keeps getting shorter and shorter. Not enough — the speed doesn't really change.

892
00:49:49,350 --> 00:49:56,730
Hmm, we need more momentum, don't we.

893
00:49:56,730 --> 00:49:59,910
Hmm...

894
00:49:59,910 --> 00:50:05,510
What do we do? What do we do?

895
00:50:05,510 --> 00:50:09,750
I have no idea.

896
00:50:09,750 --> 00:50:15,490
To accelerate... how do we take out the laser?

897
00:50:15,490 --> 00:50:19,950
What do we do with the laser? That laser thing...

898
00:50:19,950 --> 00:50:24,990
We can defeat enemies with it? How would that work?

899
00:50:24,990 --> 00:50:31,690
Whoa, it came flying in with so much speed! That momentum just now — does the momentum matter?

900
00:50:31,690 --> 00:50:40,530
But I don't think it changes — it should be the same force as the fall before. The target is always...

901
00:50:40,530 --> 00:50:44,330
The robot was doing it, right? With the laser.

902
00:50:44,330 --> 00:50:48,130
The tip of this laser...

903
00:50:48,130 --> 00:50:53,010
We can't really attach anything to the tip of the laser, can we.

904
00:50:53,010 --> 00:50:56,780
There doesn't seem to be anywhere to attach it.

905
00:50:56,780 --> 00:51:01,780
The little cube — it'd be great if we could hold it, but it doesn't seem like we can get close enough.

906
00:51:05,180 --> 00:51:10,520
Isn't that thing just floating around, unable to sink or anything?

907
00:51:10,520 --> 00:51:15,760
Wait, this isn't like... a mid-air catch situation, right? Surely not.

908
00:51:15,760 --> 00:51:17,360
You never know!

909
00:51:17,360 --> 00:51:22,040
If you catch it mid-air, how do you even carry it?

910
00:51:22,040 --> 00:51:26,860
From here, it went flying all the way over there, right?

911
00:51:26,860 --> 00:51:28,280
Yeah, that's right.

912
00:51:31,220 --> 00:51:35,720
Luna did that part, so I didn't quite catch which portals were connected.

913
00:51:35,720 --> 00:51:36,220
Huh?

914
00:51:36,220 --> 00:51:39,320
From here, Polka went flying all the way to the exit,

915
00:51:39,320 --> 00:51:42,520
and at that moment, with perfect timing, from below—

916
00:51:42,520 --> 00:51:45,320
the cube gets launched upward like this.

917
00:51:45,320 --> 00:51:47,320
That was incredibly complicated, wasn't it!

918
00:51:47,320 --> 00:51:49,620
Hey!

919
00:51:49,620 --> 00:51:50,920
This one!

920
00:51:50,920 --> 00:51:54,220
But it doesn't do anything.

921
00:51:54,220 --> 00:51:55,520
Good effort though!

922
00:51:55,520 --> 00:51:57,170
Huh~

923
00:52:00,910 --> 00:52:04,150
Hmm... circus, grand circus!

924
00:52:04,150 --> 00:52:06,150
Are you doing a grand circus act, Polka?

925
00:52:06,150 --> 00:52:08,880
Polka's gonna do an ultra, ultra grand trick!

926
00:52:08,880 --> 00:52:10,750
What do I need to do?

927
00:52:10,750 --> 00:52:16,150
But that can't be right, can it? Is it really that hard?

928
00:52:16,150 --> 00:52:18,870
How do you even do this, seriously.

929
00:52:18,870 --> 00:52:20,670
Umm...

930
00:52:20,670 --> 00:52:22,190
It's stacking up.

931
00:52:22,190 --> 00:52:27,470
Luna handles the one on the far side, and if Polka is going to do the grand circus move—

932
00:52:27,470 --> 00:52:29,470
Assuming we do the grand circus move?

933
00:52:29,470 --> 00:52:32,470
We connect this and this, right?

934
00:52:32,470 --> 00:52:34,790
Connect this and this.

935
00:52:34,790 --> 00:52:37,440
And then—

936
00:52:37,440 --> 00:52:39,880
Then—

937
00:52:39,880 --> 00:52:42,320
Umm, Polka—

938
00:52:42,320 --> 00:52:43,620
Oh but—

939
00:52:43,620 --> 00:52:47,900
Jump!

940
00:52:47,900 --> 00:52:51,580
To grab this—

941
00:52:51,580 --> 00:52:53,620
Wait, jump!

942
00:52:53,620 --> 00:52:55,360
The timing is tricky!

943
00:52:55,360 --> 00:52:56,860
How do you get the cube over there?

944
00:52:56,860 --> 00:53:03,830
Hmm, it can't really be that big of a trick, can it?

945
00:53:03,830 --> 00:53:10,960
I don't get it, I don't get it — what's going on?

946
00:53:10,960 --> 00:53:13,680
Polka, Polka, Polka, Polka!

947
00:53:13,680 --> 00:53:14,520
She's crying!

948
00:53:14,520 --> 00:53:17,580
What do we do, Polka?

949
00:53:17,580 --> 00:53:20,320
Polka has absolutely no idea either.

950
00:53:20,320 --> 00:53:24,400
Everyone — what are we supposed to do here?

951
00:53:24,400 --> 00:53:28,140
Place a portal on the ceiling on the far side.

952
00:53:28,140 --> 00:53:30,940
But it seemed like some people figured it out.

953
00:53:30,940 --> 00:53:31,940
Someone did? How do you do it?

954
00:53:31,940 --> 00:53:37,940
Polka doesn't know about using the far-side one — I left everything to Luna earlier.

955
00:53:37,940 --> 00:53:40,680
Caution!

956
00:53:40,680 --> 00:53:46,580
In the end, when we got to the exit, we connected it to that one, right?

957
00:53:46,580 --> 00:53:51,480
The jump Polka did earlier was by connecting this portal and that one.

958
00:53:51,480 --> 00:53:54,680
Yeah, yeah, yeah! I didn't know that — that's amazing.

959
00:53:54,680 --> 00:53:56,680
So with that—

960
00:53:56,680 --> 00:54:02,350
We can't get this guy to do that for us, can we.

961
00:54:02,350 --> 00:54:05,080
This thing ends up getting destroyed somewhere along the way.

962
00:54:05,080 --> 00:54:08,880
This one... maybe there's a shield over there?

963
00:54:08,880 --> 00:54:10,740
Yeah, that's the thing.

964
00:54:10,740 --> 00:54:13,480
It just disappears.

965
00:54:13,480 --> 00:54:15,280
Wait, just once.

966
00:54:15,280 --> 00:54:19,760
Hold on, didn't Polka have the cube earlier?

967
00:54:19,760 --> 00:54:26,680
It'd be nice if we could do the whole thing with just the cube.

968
00:54:26,680 --> 00:54:37,700
This...

969
00:54:37,700 --> 00:54:42,380
This...

970
00:54:42,380 --> 00:54:46,900
What do we do with it?

971
00:54:50,220 --> 00:54:58,580
Ugh... I have no idea what to do with this!

972
00:54:58,580 --> 00:55:07,220
Whoever figures it out is amazing! This... this... ah... this? Here?

973
00:55:07,220 --> 00:55:10,920
No, that can't be right — drop it right away?

974
00:55:10,920 --> 00:55:16,300
Huh? Huh? Where's it going? Huh? It stopped moving.

975
00:55:16,300 --> 00:55:19,100
So only this one won't go.

976
00:55:19,100 --> 00:55:25,600
Where are you dropping that?

977
00:55:25,600 --> 00:55:27,600
It just plopped down.

978
00:55:27,600 --> 00:55:28,400
Where'd it go?

979
00:55:28,400 --> 00:55:31,400
I was thinking it should've gone over that way.

980
00:55:31,400 --> 00:55:34,200
It doesn't have enough momentum.

981
00:55:34,200 --> 00:55:37,000
To give it momentum...

982
00:55:43,150 --> 00:55:47,150
Okay, Polka, try connecting this spot and that spot for now.

983
00:55:47,150 --> 00:55:59,700
Then you float over, and earlier Polka went like this, like this, and got killed by a turret.

984
00:55:59,700 --> 00:56:02,700
Shall we savor it — have you experienced the feeling of dying to a turret?

985
00:56:02,700 --> 00:56:04,500
I experienced it.

986
00:56:04,500 --> 00:56:06,500
Hmm...

987
00:56:06,500 --> 00:56:12,890
Well, the number of turrets here is insane — four of them.

988
00:56:12,890 --> 00:56:15,690
Four, yeah — big turrets and small turrets.

989
00:56:15,690 --> 00:56:20,690
So basically we use the laser to blast all of them at once.

990
00:56:20,690 --> 00:56:26,540
What are we supposed to do with this laser?

991
00:56:26,540 --> 00:56:32,370
The laser... ugh, the laser...

992
00:56:32,370 --> 00:56:40,040
The cube can't get past here.

993
00:56:40,040 --> 00:56:42,040
Right, the cube can't get past.

994
00:56:43,040 --> 00:56:46,840
And the laser is angled slightly to the left.

995
00:56:46,840 --> 00:56:48,840
Oh, does it work here?

996
00:56:48,840 --> 00:56:50,640
Is that it?

997
00:56:50,640 --> 00:56:53,240
Do we do it here?

998
00:56:53,240 --> 00:56:55,250
Luna.

999
00:56:55,250 --> 00:56:57,050
Do what?

1000
00:56:57,050 --> 00:56:59,970
Refract it there?

1001
00:56:59,970 --> 00:57:01,850
How do you refract it? With this?

1002
00:57:01,850 --> 00:57:02,850
No idea.

1003
00:57:02,850 --> 00:57:04,650
Isn't it impossible?

1004
00:57:04,650 --> 00:57:05,650
Impossible.

1005
00:57:05,650 --> 00:57:07,250
But we'll do it anyway.

1006
00:57:07,250 --> 00:57:09,200
Huh, where'd it go?

1007
00:57:09,200 --> 00:57:15,590
I feel like this door is probably the same deal.

1008
00:57:15,590 --> 00:57:19,850
Can't we cover the side wall with orange? What does that even mean?

1009
00:57:19,850 --> 00:57:22,930
Cover the side wall with orange gel?

1010
00:57:22,930 --> 00:57:26,370
I don't think you can place portals where the laser is.

1011
00:57:26,370 --> 00:57:28,050
Can't refract it.

1012
00:57:28,050 --> 00:57:29,470
Polka brought it over.

1013
00:57:29,470 --> 00:57:32,670
But it'll get destroyed, right?

1014
00:57:32,670 --> 00:57:34,670
It'll break, won't it?

1015
00:57:34,670 --> 00:57:39,110
Ah, destroyed. So fragile.

1016
00:57:39,110 --> 00:57:45,710
It gets destroyed. So that means we don't carry it through here.

1017
00:57:45,710 --> 00:57:53,990
There are still unpainted spots. Still? How do we paint from the side? Paint everything? Paint everything?

1018
00:57:53,990 --> 00:57:58,430
I thought I'd painted it all. Still more? Here? Can we paint this?

1019
00:57:58,430 --> 00:58:04,010
Hmm, but that part's tricky, isn't it...

1020
00:58:04,010 --> 00:58:11,000
Hmm...

1021
00:58:11,000 --> 00:58:17,800
Ugh, I can't paint it!

1022
00:58:17,800 --> 00:58:20,770
Lukewarm~

1023
00:58:20,770 --> 00:58:25,050
Lukewarm~ But we painted quite a lot, right?

1024
00:58:25,050 --> 00:58:30,770
Hmm, does painting around here even matter? Oh, go ahead, go ahead.

1025
00:58:30,770 --> 00:58:33,500
There!

1026
00:58:33,500 --> 00:58:43,600
Maybe you can stand on this? No, I already did that spot, and the hole on the left, and the one above it too.

1027
00:58:43,600 --> 00:58:51,760
You didn't, you didn't — it's fine. You only flicked a tiny drop on it.

1028
00:58:51,760 --> 00:58:59,120
What's going on here? Oh, that's already done. Then where's the rest?

1029
00:58:59,120 --> 00:59:06,790
Like this one. Hmm.

1030
00:59:06,790 --> 00:59:13,030
Oh wait, that earlier thing was wrong. Oh, I already did that one. Yeah.

1031
00:59:13,030 --> 00:59:21,220
What if you paint right here? Yeah.

1032
00:59:21,220 --> 00:59:24,920
I want to paint here. Luna, I want to paint here.

1033
00:59:24,920 --> 00:59:26,720
Mm.

1034
00:59:26,720 --> 00:59:33,720
What's the point of that spot anyway?

1035
00:59:33,720 --> 00:59:38,860
If only there were a gel route there...

1036
00:59:38,860 --> 00:59:44,580
Aaaaaah!

1037
00:59:44,580 --> 00:59:48,880
Whoa — I got it! Waaah!

1038
00:59:48,880 --> 00:59:51,400
It went this way! Huh?

1039
00:59:51,400 --> 00:59:53,910
There!

1040
00:59:53,910 --> 00:59:56,490
Got it!

1041
00:59:56,490 --> 01:00:06,350
It keeps flying out! That spot doesn't work, does it? That's impossible, right? This, this... isn't this some kind of sign?

1042
01:00:06,350 --> 01:00:12,450
Is this wet? No? So where does this go?

1043
01:00:12,750 --> 01:00:14,750
Let's just hold on for a sec.

1044
01:00:14,750 --> 01:00:21,230
Does painting it a different color change anything?

1045
01:00:21,230 --> 01:00:24,310
Nope, nothing changes.

1046
01:00:24,310 --> 01:00:25,990
Really?

1047
01:00:25,990 --> 01:00:27,590
The portal... ah, that won't work.

1048
01:00:27,590 --> 01:00:29,590
Whoops, splat!

1049
01:00:29,590 --> 01:00:35,560
Like this...

1050
01:00:35,560 --> 01:00:36,200
What the heck!

1051
01:00:36,200 --> 01:00:38,000
Jump out of here and...

1052
01:00:38,000 --> 01:00:39,800
Delete it.

1053
01:00:39,800 --> 01:00:41,600
Oh wait, that's pointless.

1054
01:00:41,600 --> 01:00:44,200
I went whoops and splat again.

1055
01:00:44,220 --> 01:00:51,140
If Luna-tan were at that bouncy spot...

1056
01:00:51,140 --> 01:00:56,920
Even if she were, without enough momentum you can't stop it.

1057
01:00:56,920 --> 01:01:00,880
Someone needs to be here...

1058
01:01:00,880 --> 01:01:04,540
And by "someone" I obviously mean Polka.

1059
01:01:04,540 --> 01:01:09,270
Ah! Aren't you supposed to give a thumbs up?

1060
01:01:09,270 --> 01:01:10,270
Yeah.

1061
01:01:10,270 --> 01:01:19,110
Right, I thought so. It says something like "refract the laser" right here.

1062
01:01:19,110 --> 01:01:27,110
So probably the ball comes out from here, falls down...

1063
01:01:27,110 --> 01:01:30,220
Wait, the ball!

1064
01:01:30,220 --> 01:01:31,520
Yep.

1065
01:01:31,520 --> 01:01:33,220
Come on, ball!

1066
01:01:33,220 --> 01:01:34,030
Okay.

1067
01:01:34,320 --> 01:01:41,920
The ball comes and I can't catch the orb at this height. It's too low.

1068
01:01:41,920 --> 01:01:47,520
Then what about here?

1069
01:01:47,520 --> 01:01:51,260
Is that it?

1070
01:01:51,260 --> 01:01:55,080
Wait.

1071
01:01:55,080 --> 01:01:56,080
What was that just now?

1072
01:01:56,080 --> 01:02:01,680
If I put it here, I can catch the orb while jumping.

1073
01:02:02,480 --> 01:02:06,610
I can catch it! I can catch it!

1074
01:02:06,610 --> 01:02:09,410
And I can even catch it from the other side!

1075
01:02:09,410 --> 01:02:13,810
Catch it, then use that momentum to go from here...

1076
01:02:13,810 --> 01:02:15,620
Wait, hold on, that...

1077
01:02:15,620 --> 01:02:18,610
Can't we use that momentum to move over here?

1078
01:02:18,610 --> 01:02:22,430
So Luna-tan, if you move the red portal from here to here...

1079
01:02:22,430 --> 01:02:30,000
Ah, but... wait?

1080
01:02:30,000 --> 01:02:31,900
No wait, something's off, like one more step...

1081
01:02:31,900 --> 01:02:32,800
Refraction!

1082
01:02:32,800 --> 01:02:34,800
Because it needs to be refracted.

1083
01:02:34,800 --> 01:02:38,600
After catching it directly, what move do we make next?

1084
01:02:38,600 --> 01:02:40,600
Right, right, right, right.

1085
01:02:40,600 --> 01:02:46,220
Like, use the catching momentum to go straight down?

1086
01:02:46,220 --> 01:02:50,250
Don't be ridiculous!

1087
01:02:50,250 --> 01:02:56,250
Jump in here, use the momentum from landing, then bounce up from below like boing!

1088
01:02:56,250 --> 01:02:58,250
Even the Great Circus act can't pull that off, that's way too much.

1089
01:02:58,250 --> 01:03:04,050
Probably Luna-tan just switches it quickly like bam-bam-bam, and the ball just flies on its own.

1090
01:03:04,850 --> 01:03:08,650
First catch it, then just let it fly.

1091
01:03:08,650 --> 01:03:13,270
The question is where exactly do we do the catch, right?

1092
01:03:13,270 --> 01:03:17,070
Grab this one — boing!

1093
01:03:17,070 --> 01:03:21,090
The timing is tricky.

1094
01:03:21,090 --> 01:03:25,600
Ready, go!

1095
01:03:25,600 --> 01:03:29,690
Go where?

1096
01:03:29,690 --> 01:03:33,090
Ah, we need to be faster.

1097
01:03:34,180 --> 01:03:38,180
Move faster. Hmm, this is tough.

1098
01:03:38,180 --> 01:03:39,920
Wait, hold on, that just now.

1099
01:03:39,920 --> 01:03:41,790
We caught it, but...?

1100
01:03:41,790 --> 01:03:44,720
I think Luna-tan needs to instantly move it over here right away.

1101
01:03:44,720 --> 01:03:45,720
Yeah, you're right.

1102
01:03:45,720 --> 01:03:47,520
From here to here. Wait.

1103
01:03:47,520 --> 01:03:50,320
If we just do what we just did but faster.

1104
01:03:50,320 --> 01:03:52,320
The circus performer is just running right now.

1105
01:03:52,320 --> 01:03:54,920
So we hit the switch and do it immediately?

1106
01:03:54,920 --> 01:04:00,720
Press here, quickly hit the switch, complete the transfer, and then — like this!

1107
01:04:00,720 --> 01:04:01,980
That's it!

1108
01:04:01,980 --> 01:04:03,040
Got it!

1109
01:04:03,040 --> 01:04:05,070
Looks like we can make it on this side.

1110
01:04:05,070 --> 01:04:07,640
Let's go for it!

1111
01:04:07,640 --> 01:04:11,140
3, 2, 1, go!

1112
01:04:11,140 --> 01:04:14,810
Will we make it in time? It's not stopping...

1113
01:04:14,810 --> 01:04:16,210
Sorry, I was a little too early.

1114
01:04:16,210 --> 01:04:17,410
Wait, wait!

1115
01:04:17,410 --> 01:04:19,670
Luna-tan was too fast and...

1116
01:04:19,670 --> 01:04:20,590
The ball...

1117
01:04:20,590 --> 01:04:24,690
Ball transport failed.

1118
01:04:24,690 --> 01:04:25,570
It's okay!

1119
01:04:25,570 --> 01:04:27,150
Sorry, sorry!

1120
01:04:27,150 --> 01:04:29,150
Oh, but wait — that was actually really good just now!

1121
01:04:29,150 --> 01:04:34,150
That was great! Can you even do it mid-air? Is that a thing here?

1122
01:04:34,150 --> 01:04:39,750
Mid-air you probably just catch the bullet, right? Boing boing.

1123
01:04:39,750 --> 01:04:40,550
Yeah.

1124
01:04:40,550 --> 01:04:42,350
Let's try again.

1125
01:04:42,350 --> 01:04:44,350
So mid-air we really just catch the bullet?

1126
01:04:44,350 --> 01:04:48,950
There's no way we have to catch it mid-air and kill them with it, right?

1127
01:04:48,950 --> 01:04:49,750
Okay.

1128
01:04:49,750 --> 01:04:50,750
Let's go!

1129
01:04:50,750 --> 01:04:52,550
Let's try it once after.

1130
01:04:52,550 --> 01:04:53,550
Here we go!

1131
01:04:53,550 --> 01:04:55,350
3, 2, 1... okay!

1132
01:04:55,350 --> 01:04:58,930
Yes!

1133
01:04:58,930 --> 01:05:00,530
Got it!

1134
01:05:00,530 --> 01:05:01,330
I got it!

1135
01:05:01,330 --> 01:05:04,330
Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah!

1136
01:05:04,330 --> 01:05:10,910
Just now! Something just happened! Wait, does this mean we have to defeat them mid-air?!

1137
01:05:10,910 --> 01:05:11,910
Are you serious?!

1138
01:05:11,910 --> 01:05:12,910
No way!

1139
01:05:12,910 --> 01:05:14,910
Oh come on, come on, come on!

1140
01:05:14,910 --> 01:05:18,510
But just now, something was going really well!

1141
01:05:18,510 --> 01:05:22,110
That was SO close just now!

1142
01:05:22,110 --> 01:05:25,110
Wait, so we can't do it mid-air like that?

1143
01:05:25,110 --> 01:05:28,110
We can't, but that's the only hit point there is.

1144
01:05:28,110 --> 01:05:30,710
Huh?

1145
01:05:30,710 --> 01:05:32,510
Huh?

1146
01:05:32,510 --> 01:05:34,310
Huh?

1147
01:05:34,310 --> 01:05:37,110
Are there two floors?

1148
01:05:37,110 --> 01:05:38,710
Wait, what do you mean?

1149
01:05:38,710 --> 01:05:40,510
That was crazy just now.

1150
01:05:40,510 --> 01:05:44,510
So when they come here, we do it this way next time?

1151
01:05:44,510 --> 01:05:52,870
I'll transport them and...

1152
01:05:53,670 --> 01:05:54,670
Huh?

1153
01:05:54,670 --> 01:06:00,470
After transporting, Polka goes like this and jumps—

1154
01:06:00,470 --> 01:06:02,270
Like this?

1155
01:06:02,270 --> 01:06:06,220
Hmm, can we actually do it this way?

1156
01:06:06,220 --> 01:06:12,550
Let's try again.

1157
01:06:12,550 --> 01:06:14,350
So that's where the button is—

1158
01:06:14,350 --> 01:06:18,350
Is that there for the group of 3 and the 1?

1159
01:06:18,350 --> 01:06:20,150
No idea.

1160
01:06:20,150 --> 01:06:22,150
Will it loop infinitely?

1161
01:06:22,150 --> 01:06:24,950
Will it become an infinite bounce loop?

1162
01:06:24,950 --> 01:06:31,750
We'll give it a shot. Because those 3 and 1 are right where those guys are, you know.

1163
01:06:31,750 --> 01:06:32,750
Yeah, you're right.

1164
01:06:32,750 --> 01:06:34,480
Alright, let's go!

1165
01:06:34,480 --> 01:06:36,350
3, 2, 1, GO!

1166
01:06:36,350 --> 01:06:40,000
Transport complete.

1167
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:40,950
Here they come.

1168
01:06:40,950 --> 01:06:41,950
Jump, and—there.

1169
01:06:41,950 --> 01:06:46,470
What just happened? What's going on?

1170
01:06:46,470 --> 01:06:47,810
They're flying, they're flying!

1171
01:06:47,810 --> 01:06:49,930
What's happening now?

1172
01:06:49,930 --> 01:06:51,590
It's an infinite bounce loop!

1173
01:06:51,590 --> 01:06:53,350
It's an infinite bounce loop!

1174
01:06:53,350 --> 01:06:55,190
We haven't taken them down yet.

1175
01:06:55,190 --> 01:06:57,030
Got one!

1176
01:06:57,030 --> 01:06:58,570
Got one!

1177
01:06:58,570 --> 01:07:00,770
That last one over there!

1178
01:07:00,770 --> 01:07:01,550
Nice, nice!

1179
01:07:01,550 --> 01:07:05,050
This turned into an action game!

1180
01:07:05,050 --> 01:07:06,410
We haven't taken them all down yet.

1181
01:07:06,410 --> 01:07:07,710
Still haven't gotten them all.

1182
01:07:07,710 --> 01:07:10,380
Did we get them all?!

1183
01:07:10,380 --> 01:07:20,210
Whoa— wait, huh? Did we get them? Did we? Did we do it?!

1184
01:07:20,210 --> 01:07:30,130
But I can't hear their voices anymore... wait, something's still bouncing... oh, nice nice nice, looks like we got them! Oh, they're gone! The right one got obliterated!

1185
01:07:30,130 --> 01:07:37,610
The left one too, I think we did it! Is this okay now? Did we clear it? Oh, we might've done it!

1186
01:07:37,610 --> 01:07:46,630
We did it! We did it! We did it! Aaaaaah! Wait, this thing isn't human — it's alive now?!

1187
01:07:46,630 --> 01:07:58,630
Woohoo! Oh I see, I see! Really?! So that's how it works?! That's insane! Polka, you're amazing!

1188
01:07:58,630 --> 01:08:14,620
So as a reward, I just have to keep jumping now? Yeah! Let's go! Woo! Yay! Woo! Yay! Will this work? Won't I get shot? Nope, you won't get shot! I'm not getting shot!

1189
01:08:14,620 --> 01:08:17,450
Nope, you won't get shot!

1190
01:08:17,450 --> 01:08:22,450
Yes! So Polka just needs to repaint it?

1191
01:08:22,450 --> 01:08:28,170
Yeah, exactly! Let's go, waaah!

1192
01:08:28,170 --> 01:08:32,930
Waaah! Here we go!

1193
01:08:32,930 --> 01:08:37,290
Yay!

1194
01:08:37,290 --> 01:08:42,010
Man, that was tough. There's so much you can't figure out until you actually try it.

1195
01:08:42,010 --> 01:08:44,770
Without even thinking, it just moves like that?

1196
01:08:44,770 --> 01:08:48,150
The infinite bounce loop appeared again!

1197
01:08:48,150 --> 01:08:56,460
Next up — Dead Seven!

1198
01:08:56,460 --> 01:09:00,360
It looks simple, but simple ones are always the hardest.

1199
01:09:00,360 --> 01:09:03,820
Right now, this one's hard.

1200
01:09:03,820 --> 01:09:06,160
There's nothing that isn't hard.

1201
01:09:06,160 --> 01:09:10,060
There was nothing that wasn't difficult.

1202
01:09:10,820 --> 01:09:12,120
Boing boing boiing~

1203
01:09:12,120 --> 01:09:15,020
Whoa, whoa!

1204
01:09:15,020 --> 01:09:16,220
Whoa, whoa! Whoa, that's amazing!

1205
01:09:16,220 --> 01:09:18,160
My whole view turned orange!

1206
01:09:18,160 --> 01:09:21,060
There's so much ink!

1207
01:09:21,060 --> 01:09:22,760
The ink is flying everywhere!

1208
01:09:22,760 --> 01:09:24,800
Painting everything is...

1209
01:09:24,800 --> 01:09:26,320
...proper etiquette.

1210
01:09:26,320 --> 01:09:30,000
Oh, so you place the cube here.

1211
01:09:30,000 --> 01:09:32,920
Oh, there's one over here too.

1212
01:09:32,920 --> 01:09:34,020
I got a straight line here!

1213
01:09:34,020 --> 01:09:35,900
Oh, looks like I can jump super high!

1214
01:09:35,900 --> 01:09:37,260
Amazing!

1215
01:09:37,260 --> 01:09:38,300
Wait, we jump really high?

1216
01:09:38,300 --> 01:09:43,300
WHOOOA! We collided! We crashed into each other!

1217
01:09:43,300 --> 01:09:45,100
WHOOOA!

1218
01:09:45,100 --> 01:09:48,900
I was trying to tackle Polka. That was scary.

1219
01:09:48,900 --> 01:09:53,700
WHOOOA! I'm gonna tackle you!

1220
01:09:53,700 --> 01:09:55,500
Huh? What is this?

1221
01:09:55,500 --> 01:09:58,300
If I do this, the top... What did you do?

1222
01:09:58,300 --> 01:10:02,300
Doesn't it come out from above? The ball comes out from here.

1223
01:10:02,300 --> 01:10:06,100
Oh, the ball comes out from there — wait, it doesn't. It does, it doesn't.

1224
01:10:06,100 --> 01:10:10,970
What is this? The ball isn't getting caught!

1225
01:10:10,970 --> 01:10:12,770
Hmm?

1226
01:10:12,770 --> 01:10:15,570
This thing has no intention of getting on top of that.

1227
01:10:15,570 --> 01:10:20,800
What is this ball doing, it just falls...

1228
01:10:20,800 --> 01:10:23,800
So what are we supposed to do about that?

1229
01:10:23,800 --> 01:10:26,600
Does Polka have to go catch it again?

1230
01:10:26,600 --> 01:10:29,500
But I can't fly or anything like that.

1231
01:10:29,500 --> 01:10:33,200
You probably need momentum — jump from here, not from there.

1232
01:10:33,200 --> 01:10:36,780
I see. Well, I'm used to that much by now.

1233
01:10:36,780 --> 01:10:41,040
But how do we build up momentum here?

1234
01:10:41,040 --> 01:10:44,200
Maybe this?

1235
01:10:44,200 --> 01:10:46,860
This straight line... but hmm, but...

1236
01:10:46,860 --> 01:10:49,860
Can't we go straight into the wall?

1237
01:10:49,860 --> 01:10:51,500
Oh, use the momentum from here?

1238
01:10:51,500 --> 01:10:54,960
Don't tell me it's infinite again? Infinitely along this wall...

1239
01:10:54,960 --> 01:11:01,520
Yeah, that seems likely — the way these are lined up.

1240
01:11:01,520 --> 01:11:08,560
And then like this... infinitely... and then whoosh over here!

1241
01:11:08,560 --> 01:11:16,440
Ahaha! Ahaha! You go, but you also have to activate this side!

1242
01:11:16,440 --> 01:11:21,700
But I get it now. Polka was just daydreaming there.

1243
01:11:21,700 --> 01:11:27,600
Wait, isn't this hard? So then, hold this down...

1244
01:11:27,600 --> 01:11:30,720
Because Polka can't stop moving anymore.

1245
01:11:30,720 --> 01:11:33,480
Oh, she stopped.

1246
01:11:33,480 --> 01:11:34,930
That was a fail.

1247
01:11:34,930 --> 01:11:37,760
One more time, please!

1248
01:11:37,760 --> 01:11:43,520
Oh, no good.

1249
01:11:43,520 --> 01:11:47,380
Tokyo Friend Park!

1250
01:11:47,380 --> 01:11:50,540
This one.

1251
01:11:50,540 --> 01:11:53,640
Kana's...

1252
01:11:53,640 --> 01:11:55,120
...ball.

1253
01:11:55,120 --> 01:11:59,920
Ball, please!

1254
01:11:59,920 --> 01:12:12,010
So we're supposed to move using this here.

1255
01:12:12,010 --> 01:12:14,010
Luna had too much to deal with and came back.

1256
01:12:14,010 --> 01:12:17,010
We have to go back and forth between here and there. I see.

1257
01:12:17,010 --> 01:12:20,010
